     "type": "key",
     "style": "retenir",
     "title": "In the classroom",
     "md": "**pen**, **pencil**, **book**, **notebook**, **ruler**, **bag**, **desk**, **chair**, **blackboard**, **teacher**, **pupil**.\n\nLe corps : **head**, **arm**, **hand**, **leg**, **foot** (pluriel : **feet**), **eye**, **ear**, **nose**, **mouth**."
    },
    {
     "type": "example",
     "title": "Exemple 1 : this is / these are",
     "statement": "Complète : « (1 book) This is a book. (2 books) These … books. »",
     "steps": [
      {
       "md": "Un objet proche : **This is** a book."
      },
      {
       "md": "Plusieurs objets proches : **These are** books (on ajoute -s au nom)."
      }
     ],
     "answer": "**This is a book. These are books.**"
    },
    {
     "type": "example",
     "title": "Exemple 2 : les pluriels irréguliers",
     "statement": "Écris le pluriel de : child, foot, man.",
     "steps": [
      {
       "md": "Certains mots ne prennent pas -s."
      },
      {
       "md": "child → **children** ; foot → **feet** ; man → **men**."
      }
     ],
     "answer": "**children, feet, men.**"
    },
    {
     "type": "key",
     "style": "pieges",
     "title": "Erreurs fréquentes",
     "md": "- Dire « I have two brother » : on écrit **two brothers**.\n- Dire « my sister, he » : **she** pour une fille.\n- Écrire « childs » : le pluriel de child est **children**.\n- Confondre **this** (un seul) et **these** (plusieurs).\n- Oublier a / an : **a** book, **an** orange (devant une voyelle)."
    },
